    {
      "block_id": "2605.06070_p8_b38",
      "text": "ArenaPO vs. Uniform Margin The reward in ArenaPO is incorporated in the form of a margin.\nTherefore, we also compare it with fixed-margin baselines, as shown in Table 5, where the fixed\nmargin is the replacement of QD. It can be seen that the uniform margin yields only limited\nimprovements, while ArenaPO provides fine-grained and adaptive awards, resulting in significantly\nbetter performance. To improve the discriminability of the results, we also evaluate on the new\nbenchmark K-Sort Eval [18], and the results are presented in Appendix E.\n",
